[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Feature flags whose removal is a bead, a deadline, and a gate[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]SASE has one boolean feature-flag registry resolved through the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]existing config layer chain, every temporary flag is owned by a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]dedicated `flag` bead carrying a date-and-release removal [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]threshold, that threshold raises a FlagTriage gate the owner [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]answers with Remove / Extend / Keep / Close, flag beads read [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]unmistakably on every surface that renders a bead, and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`sase/memory/sase_flags.md` teaches agents when a flag is warranted[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and how to retire one.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]10[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]feature_flags.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/feature_flags.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-nb[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-nb/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The flag bead type in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core: add IssueTypeWire::Flag and the BeadFlagWire record to the bead [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire, mirror the snooze-record validation shape, extend every exhaustive[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]match over issue type, and give the flag type its CLI glyph and accent.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The typed registry, resolver, and snapshot[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]registry[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]registry: build the code-owned flag registry, the layered resolver and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]its immutable per-process snapshot, the strict SASE_FEATURE_FLAGS [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]transport, and the generated feature_flags block in the config JSON [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Schema.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Flag beads in the Python bead layer[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]bead[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead: mirror IssueType.FLAG and FlagRecord through the Python model, the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SQLite compatibility layer, the wire conversion, and the sase bead [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]create/show/update surfaces.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The shared flag visual language[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]look[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bead[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]look: register the flag bead type's glyph and accent, and add the shared[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead_flag_presentation module that renders the flag key chip and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]urgency-graded removal countdown for every surface.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Registry and bead integrity enforcement[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]lint[dim] · [dim][/dim]after registry, bead[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]lint: ship tools/check_feature_flags with its static registry rules and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]its bead-status rules, wire it into just lint and just validate, and ban[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]import-time flag resolution.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The FlagTriage gate and its reconciler[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]gate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after registry, look[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate: add the trusted FlagTriage gate contract with its Remove, Extend, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Keep, and Close options and host effects, and generalize the bead gate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reconciler so a due flag bead raises exactly one pending gate.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase flag and the flag doctor checks[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after registry, look[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli: add the sase flag group with list, new, and show, and register the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]flags.* doctor checks covering registry integrity, override hygiene, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]overdue flags.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Flag beads on every bead-rendering surface[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]ui[dim] · [dim][/dim]after look[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ui: render flag beads distinctly in the bead CLI rows and detail, bead [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pages, the ACE Beads pane and its modals and filters, the notification [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and gate panels, and the Telegram bead formatter, with a visual snapshot[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]golden.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The first two real flags[/bold #D7AFFF]                                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]consumer[dim] · [dim][/dim]after lint, gate, cli[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]consumer: convert one opt-in beta 